# Copy to .env.local and fill in.

# Hosts allowed to reach the dev server, so the site can be opened on a phone
# on the same network. Comma-separated, no protocol or port.
#
# Find your machine's address with:
#   ipconfig getifaddr en0        # e.g. 192.168.1.42
#   scutil --get LocalHostName    # append .local, e.g. my-laptop.local
#
# Leave unset if you only ever use localhost.
DEV_ORIGINS=

# Analytics (PostHog). Both are public — they go to the browser — and the site
# simply records nothing when they are unset, which is what local development
# wants. Provisioned on Vercel; pull them with `vercel env pull`.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN   the write-only project token, phc_...
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST            https://eu.posthog.com (or us.)
#
# Set on Vercel for Production only, so local and preview runs cannot add
# our own testing to her visitor numbers. Unset, the site records nothing.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=
